Recommended execution sequence
1. Step 1 — Architecture audit

   Give Antigravity the specification and instruct it to execute Phase 0 only.

   It should return an architecture map, existing component inventory, and proposed modification plan.
   No code changes
2. Step 2 — Visual design proposal

   Have it examine the actual UI and produce a proposed redesign, including the main window, terminal panes, navigation, drawers, and settings.

   Require screenshots or working visual previews using the existing application framework.
3. Step 3 — Design system implementation

   Implement the tokens, materials, themes, and visual configuration infrastructure.

   Verify that existing settings and configuration remain compatible.
4. Step 4 — Main interface modernization

   Redesign the application shell, terminal presentation, navigation, and workspace layout.
5. Step 5 — Remaining UI modernization

   Update drawers, floating panels, contextual menus, command palette, and settings.
6. Step 6 — Regression and polish

   Verify existing terminal functionality, session persistence, rendering performance, and visual consistency.
